1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,553
A completed FEAT report is not
automatically a valid analysis.

2
00:00:04,553 --> 00:00:07,285
It is a chain of evidence.

3
00:00:07,285 --> 00:00:11,839
Review motion and preprocessing first,
registration second, the design and

4
00:00:11,839 --> 00:00:14,571
contrasts third, and statistical inference
last.

5
00:00:14,571 --> 00:00:19,124
A failure early in the chain limits every
later conclusion.

6
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:27,303
Begin with pre-stats and ask whether
motion, masking, and preprocessing outputs

7
00:00:27,303 --> 00:00:28,394
are plausible.

8
00:00:28,394 --> 00:00:32,214
Continue to registration and inspect
anatomical correspondence.

9
00:00:32,214 --> 00:00:36,580
Then examine the design matrix, EVs, and
contrasts.

10
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:42,037
Only after those dependencies pass should
you interpret thresholded results.

11
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,942
For motion, describe the pattern and any
abrupt displacement.

12
00:00:48,942 --> 00:00:53,877
For registration, name boundaries and
locations that agree or fail.

13
00:00:53,877 --> 00:01:00,292
For design, match columns to timing files
and contrast weights to the hypothesis.

14
00:01:00,292 --> 00:01:04,240
Specific observations can be reviewed;
vague reassurance cannot.

15
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:09,560
A cope is the estimated contrast effect.

16
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:12,788
A varcope describes uncertainty in that
estimate.

17
00:01:12,788 --> 00:01:17,398
A t or z statistic standardizes evidence
relative to uncertainty.

18
00:01:17,398 --> 00:01:21,547
A thresholded map shows locations
surviving the chosen inferential

19
00:01:21,547 --> 00:01:22,008
procedure.

20
00:01:22,008 --> 00:01:26,618
Do not describe a z-statistic map as an
effect-size map.

21
00:01:29,667 --> 00:01:34,519
Finish with an explicit quality-control
judgment: pass, concern, or fail, followed

22
00:01:34,519 --> 00:01:37,165
by the observations that support it.

23
00:01:37,165 --> 00:01:40,694
Record limitations and their likely effect
on interpretation.

24
00:01:40,694 --> 00:01:47,751
The goal is not to prove that FEAT
finished; it is to decide what this run

25
00:01:47,751 --> 00:01:49,075
can defensibly support.
